    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{41}{72}$\n\nWeight each box’s blue-marble probability by $\\frac13$ and add.",
      "worked": "Each box has probability $\\frac13$ of being chosen. Let $B$ be the event that a blue marble is drawn. The conditional probabilities of blue from boxes $X$, $Y$ and $Z$ are $\\frac58$, $\\frac26$ and $\\frac34$, respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B)&=\\frac13\\left(\\frac58+\\frac26+\\frac34\\right)\\\\ P(B)&=\\frac13\\times\\frac{15+8+18}{24}\\\\ P(B)&=\\frac{41}{72}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
